      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "MIGHT have narrowed down the issue to world asset package loading while looking at logs and dumps together.\n\nMy friend may actually be going through 2 bugs, but both occur around world asset package loading steps from the logs. SuspendThread SEEMS to occur either at startup OR if there's a failure in the GC pass right before loading a new world (the latter im not sure, might just be at startup TBC), and the Null Pointer hard crash SEEMS to occur *during* world asset bundle loading.\n\nHowever, for the second Null Pointer error thing, the crash is somewhat random. Sometimes it happens, sometimes it doesn't. Sometimes it happens during asset bundle loading, sometimes very shortly after it (per log lines, meaning it might still be ongoing idk how the logs treat a line). The error SEEMS to be rarer when downloading is required vs loading from cache. We haven't been able to test but all crashes seem to be around loading asset bundles. The only time a crash occured outside of loading an asset bundle is very very close to startup (the logs are like 17 lines) and stop right before the initialization of [AssetBundleDownloadManager] (this is also I believe the log of my friend's very first hard crash from SuspendThread, which matches the OP \"Happened upon launch\")\n\nIf anyone can corroborate these findings or disprove them (do your logs of a crash end abruptly really close to anything involving asset bundle loading or management?), this might help. Again, no testing yet but repeatedly manually emptying the content cache may work. Also, to dispel the idea of corrupted data (to an extent), I have one log where a specific world is downloaded and successfully joined, and a later log on the same day of joining the world and crashing on loading the asset bundle that had just been downloaded and used successfully.\n\nWonder if EAC or other low-level softwares are messing with world files.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
